:::dialect Dialect note
@office_us Office US (Low-Context): Max 1 factual reason, 0 apologies, downward FM DJ pitch on repeats.
@personal_us Personal US: Lead with 1 beat of genuine warmth so a clean boundary protects the bond.
@rioplatense Rioplatense (High-Involvement): Cushion clean boundaries with explicit warmth so steadiness never lands like ice.
@espana España: Direct, crisp, cordial—no over-apology or convoluted corporate hedging.
:::

:::dialect Clean No
@office_us "I can't take on the review tonight—my evening is booked. I can look at it tomorrow at 10."
@personal_us "I love that you asked. I'm going to pass tonight—coffee Sunday?"
@rioplatense "¡Qué lindo que me invites! Hoy paso, pero arreglemos para el domingo."
@espana "Gracias por contar conmigo; hoy no puedo ir, pero nos vemos el domingo."
:::

:::dialect Fogging line
@office_us "You're right it's a tight week, and I still can't take on the review tonight."
@personal_us "I hear it's been a while since we went out, and I care about seeing you—I'm still going to pass tonight."
@rioplatense "Tenés razón que viene brava la semana, y te quiero dar una mano, pero hoy posta no puedo agarrar la revisión."
@espana "Tienes razón en que vamos justos, y aun así hoy no puedo asumir la revisión. Mañana a las 10 sí."
:::

:::dialect Upward check
@office_us "I want to support your goal on X; I noticed we finalized Y—am I missing a constraint?"
@personal_us "I love that you handled the reservation—next time can we pick the spot together?"
@rioplatense "Che, me alegra que lo hayas armado—para la próxima, ¿elegimos el lugar juntos?"
@espana "Me parece genial que lo reservaras; la próxima vez lo elegimos juntos, ¿te viene bien?"
:::
